acceptance_criteria: Pin the current first-party SDK toolchain with refreshed lockfiles.; Prove registered policy commands and typed refusals on plain trackers and preserve published dependency bullets.; Pass package release gates and verify the committed build.
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T18:52:21.185Z","harness:claude-code","Finished by the orchestrator after the agent's provider login was revoked mid-run. On pm-cli 2026.11.24 the host evaluates beforeMutation guards during preview as well as commit and passes actor and dry_run. dedupe.ts adapts the close guard: a preview (dry_run) neither records nor consumes a pending closure, and a pending closure is bound to the author that requested it, so another actor cannot consume it; receipt, revision and deadline are still checked on commit. Tests in dedupe, cost-policy, counterfactual and replay-command follow the declared options and the new guard context. All four changelog entry points pass --dependency-updates. Orchestrator gates on the committed tree: build, typecheck, lint, changelog:check, 59/59 in the four touched test files, the changelog-flag and release-workflow tests. The full npm and Bun release gates were not run locally: CI certifies them on the PR."
